        "source": "manual_review",
        "cve_id": null,
        "description": "Resembles SQL injection: the admin user search reads attacker-controlled request.GET 'q' and 'role' values and feeds them into a database filter, which a scanner may flag as tainted input reaching a query. It is actually safe because the values are passed to the Django ORM via QuerySet.filter() with Q(username__icontains=query) and filter(role=role); the ORM parameterizes all values, so the user input becomes bound query parameters, never concatenated SQL. No raw(), extra(), or string formatting is used."
